            "text": "A flaw was found in the Linux kernel's network scheduler component. A remote attacker could send specially crafted network packets containing nested Virtual Local Area Network (VLAN) headers. This could cause the kernel to read beyond allocated memory, leading to a system crash and a denial of service.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "kernel: net: sched: act_csum: validate nested VLAN headers",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
