            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in the Linux kernel's IPv6 (Internet Protocol version 6) implementation. This vulnerability, a Use-After-Free (UAF) error, occurs due to incorrect caching of network packet addresses before a memory operation. An attacker could potentially exploit this flaw to cause memory corruption, which may lead to a denial of service or, in some scenarios, arbitrary code execution.",
