        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in webpack-dev-server. When a user configures a proxy with a broad context, such as '/', and enables WebSocket (ws: true) forwarding, the development server's own Hot Module Replacement (HMR) WebSocket can be intercepted. This interception leads to the leakage of the browser's cookies and Origin header to the proxy target, bypassing the server's Host/Origin validation. Additionally, it can corrupt the HMR socket, resulting in a denial of service for the HMR functionality.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "webpack-dev-server: webpack-dev-server: Information disclosure and denial of service via improper proxy configuration",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
        ],
